---
// About (trust page). Copy adapted from the sheet's "Start here" tab (owner decision,
// 15 Nov 2026): no name or company, no "Found via" line, no Ctrl+F tip, no WhatsApp
// channel until one exists. Includes the one-line privacy note (spec 6.7).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Graduate Radar is, how openings are found and checked, and how often the list is updated."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Graduate Radar</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A free, checked list of graduate trainee programmes, entry-level jobs and free tech trainings
      for Nigerian graduates.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>New openings are added every Tuesday and Friday morning, and closed ones are marked.</li>
      <li>Every listing links to the employer's or provider's own page wherever possible.</li>
      <li>
        Listings that look suspicious are checked first and left out if they can't be confirmed.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you'll find</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/">Jobs</a>: graduate trainee programmes, graduate internships, entry-level and
        NYSC roles in Nigeria, plus remote roles open to people in Nigeria.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/trainings">Trainings and scholarships</a>: free or low-cost tech trainings and
        tech scholarships (software, data, design, product, cloud, cybersecurity, AI).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to read a listing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Closing soon</strong> means it closes within 7 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rolling deadline</strong> means there is no fixed closing date.
        <strong>Deadline not stated</strong> means the posting didn't say, so apply early.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Who can apply</strong> (degree class, age, NYSC): check these first so you only
        apply where you qualify.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Checked</strong> is the last date we confirmed the opening was real and still open.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Stay safe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Never pay money to apply</strong> for a job or to "secure" a place.
      </li>
      <li>Apply only through the Apply link or the organisation's official website.</li>
      <li>If anyone asks you for a fee, stop and don't send money.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href="/stay-safe">How to spot a fake job</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Good to know</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't hire or process applications. We gather openings in one place.</li>
      <li>
        Details can change after we check them, so always confirm on the organisation's page before
        applying.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses no cookies and collects no personal data. Cloudflare counts page visits without
      cookies, so we can see which pages are read.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-rule);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
  }
  ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }
  .prose a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--tap-min);
  }
  li a {
    display: inline;
  }
</style>
